# [1].map(double)
# One function of the library runs for all calls of Array.prototype.map (runtimefunction 66), so it is entered with operands nobody knows, and it calls the callback among them.
# The records of map have handed `double` the element where the call is. Nothing in this program is code that nobody compiles: no such code writes anything,
# neither the array nor `double` is in unknown hands, and `double` gets the number and nothing else.
# Without records: unknown-callback-in-library-code-that-no-record-describes-is-unknown-code.ir
